From: Venus CF6 <cf6@localhost>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: set IRIS1 encoder output buffer size

Android Q sends HFI property 0x20100c with the negotiated encoder CAPTURE
plane size after it obtains buffer requirements and before it prepares
internal buffers.  It calls this property BUFFER_SIZE_MINIMUM.  Venus
already exposes the same wire ID and two-u32 BUFFER_SIZE_ACTUAL payload.
Only the decoder uses its existing helper.

Send the exact firmware-backed encoder CAPTURE allocation size after the
single post-count requirements snapshot validates both queues.  Send it
before any internal buffer is registered.  At 640x480 H.264 this is the
already verified 230400-byte contract.  Limit the change to the IRIS1
encoder-specific path.

Signed-off-by: Venus CF6 <cf6@localhost>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
index b67f1a1c6..5673f2ba4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
@@ -470,6 +470,17 @@ static int intbufs_alloc_iris1_encoder(struct venus_inst *inst)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Downstream calls this BUFFER_SIZE_MINIMUM; Venus names the same
+	 * 0x20100c two-u32 wire property BUFFER_SIZE_ACTUAL.  Tell firmware the
+	 * exact compressed CAPTURE extent before registering internal buffers.
+	 */
+	ret = venus_helper_set_bufsize(inst,
+				       inst->output_buf_size,
+				       HFI_BUFFER_OUTPUT);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(intbuf_types_4xx); i++) {
 		req = intbufs_find_req(&snapshot, intbuf_types_4xx[i]);
 		if (!req || !req->size)
